Libraries the project brings in. An external library may be given
a very high index, so a reader can skip it.

Each single-file copy sits beside a <file>.upstream note: its source, the
source's commit at copy time, the date, and what this project changed
(docs/vendored-code.md). scripts/refresh-vendored copies them again.
- llama-chat-client.lua: the llama.cpp client, from delta-version, with an
  endpoint record per call and an embedding call (issue 401b).
- dkjson.lua: the JSON reader and writer it uses.
- ensure-ram-tiers.lua, ensure-ram-tiers: the RAM folders under tmp/.
- bitmap-font.lua: the 8x8 letter pictures the Lua window draws with, from
  every-software-image-able (issue 802).
- noble-ciphers/, noble-hashes/: AES-256-GCM and PBKDF2 in plain JavaScript,
  for the HTML page, from the npm registry (issue 803; their .upstream notes).
